# ccp1d history: one line per RF period (period 0 = initial state)
# 1 period  2 t[s]  3 N_e  4 N_i  5 <n_e>[m^-3]  6 <n_i>[m^-3]  7 n_e_center[m^-3]  8 n_i_center[m^-3]
# 9 Gi_L[m^-2s^-1] 10 Gi_R 11 Ge_L 12 Ge_R  13 Ei_L[eV] 14 Ei_R[eV]  15 P_e[W/m^2] 16 P_i[W/m^2] 17 P_VI[W/m^2]
# 18 n_ioniz 19 n_exc  20 KE_e[J/m^2] 21 KE_i[J/m^2] 22 W_field[J/m^2] 23 E_wall_cum[J/m^2] 24 Work_cum[J/m^2]
# 25 gauss_res_max  26 wall[s]  27 Tx_e[eV] 28 Tperp_e[eV] 29 Tx_i[eV] 30 Tperp_i[eV]  31 numax_exceed
# Tx = m<vx^2>/e, Tperp = m<vy^2+vz^2>/(2e): temperatures of a Maxwellian with the same mean energies
# P_e, P_i = work of the field on the species (exact); P_VI = <V I> of the external circuit (Shockley-Ramo current)
# centre density = mean of the 5 central nodes at the end of the period; fluxes, energies, power = period averages;
# KE with vx at t-dt/2 (after the push), exact identity: KE_e+KE_i - KE(0) = Work_cum - E_wall_cum
